config TOF_M2462
	tristate "Infineon M2462 (IRS2975C) dual-stream ToF imager"
	depends on I2C
	help
	  Register and module-flash access for the Infineon M2462 ToF imager,
	  i.e. the IRS2975C "spot" (Flood + Spot) dual-stream modules.

	  The register map is the M2459/M2462 generation: the SPI bus master
	  is at 0xA095..0xA09A and the idle flag is STATUS0 (0x940E), not the
	  M2453/M2455/M2457 0x9403.  The driver also waits for STATUS0 before
	  enabling the SPI controller.

	  At probe time the driver reads the small Zwetschge tables (ToC,
	  TableOfRegisterMaps, TableOfUseCases) and caches every use case's
	  dense register block from the module's own SPI flash.  Selecting a
	  use case then is a pure RAM -> imager I2C burst write; no userspace
	  blob and no flash access on the hot path.

	  A dual-stream use case describes two streams that arrive in
	  alternating UVC frames.  The parser therefore exposes the raw frames
	  of one UVC frame (9 for Hybrid_Mode18), not the 18 raw frames of the
	  whole depth frame.

	  The ~200 kB calibration blob is deliberately left to userspace
	  (the depth engine input), it is never read by this driver.

	  The i2c_driver registration at the end of tof_m2462_core.c is wrapped
	  in #if 0 so the engine can be integrated into a board driver without
	  registering a second i2c driver.  Remove that guard for a standalone
	  module (and adjust the probe/remove signatures to the target kernel).

	  To compile this as a module, choose M here: the module will be
	  called tof_m2462.
